    "statistical_conclusion": "Under matched signals, S crossed threshold in 5/5 runs vs 0/5 for C on the validation split. Because observations are paired by model seed, the primary two-sided exact McNemar test yields p = 0.0625 (nonsignificant at alpha = 0.05); a directional one-sided test yields p = 0.0312 (conditional on a non-preregistered directional hypothesis). An unpaired Fisher exact test yields one-sided p = 0.0040 (two-sided p = 0.0079), though its independence assumption is violated. At epoch 50 (held-out test split), counterfactual accuracy difference (S - C) is +4.63% (paired t(4) = 2.10, two-sided p = 0.1035). Exploratory epoch-1 accuracy differences indicate an initial linear lead on both validation (+25.94%, paired t=5.41, p=0.0056) and held-out test splits."
